				\begin{document}$${\mathrm{JSD}}(P_{\alpha G},\,P_{\alpha G{\prime}})$$\end{document}JSD(PαG,PαG′) measures the difference between the α-centrality values of the signaling networks. w1, w2, and w3 are the weights of each term with w1 + w2 + w3 = 1. Similar to a previous study91, we selected w1 = 0.45, w2 = 0.45, and w3 = 0.1. The structural similarity S was computed by one minus dissimilarity measure D.
